I’m using a single-pass implementation with two explicit state variables: the number of pending spaces and the output accumulated so far. This handles runs of any length exactly as the prose says (one underscore per 1–2 spaces, one hyphen for an entire run of 3+), and the loop state admits a structural induction over the remaining character sequence.
